# Sharing your data

Nocturne gives you a few ways to let someone else see your data, each built for
a different situation — a one-off clinic visit, an always-on screen at daycare,
a person who needs their own ongoing login, or a glucose clock you can leave on
any screen. This page explains what each one does and when to reach for it; each
one then has its own page with the step-by-step detail.

All of them but the clock are managed in one place: **Settings > Sharing &
Privacy**. That page is where you switch the public link on or off, hand out
guest links, see everyone you have invited along with what each of them is
allowed to do, and choose whether people may ask you for access. Clocks are their
own thing, kept in the **Clock** section. Nothing is shared until you turn it on,
and you can revoke any of it at any time.

Public access sits at the top of the page; invites, guest links and your list of
members follow below it:

<Screenshot id="sharing-settings" />

## At a glance

| Option | Best for | Needs a login? | Expires |
|--------|----------|----------------|---------|
| [Temporary guest link](/docs/sharing/guest-links) | A one-off look — a clinic visit | No | After 48 hours, one use |
| [Public share link](/docs/sharing/public-link) | An always-on screen — a daycare | No | Never (until you turn it off) |
| [Member account](/docs/sharing/members) | An ongoing helper — a teacher or nurse | Yes | Never (until you remove them) |
| [Clock](/docs/sharing/clock) | An at-a-glance glucose screen — a bedside clock | No | Never (until you delete it) |

There is also a fifth setting that isn't a way of sharing so much as a way of
being asked: **membership requests**. Turn it on and visitors can request a
member account instead of waiting for you to send them an invite. See
[Member accounts and invites](/docs/sharing/members#membership-requests).

## Which should I use?

- **One-off, short-lived look** (a single appointment) →
  [temporary guest link](/docs/sharing/guest-links). It cleans itself up 48 hours
  after you make it and can only be used once.
- **A screen lots of people glance at** (a daycare, a classroom display) →
  [public share link](/docs/sharing/public-link), with the fewest categories you
  can manage and the 24-hour window on.
- **A named person who needs ongoing access** (a regular clinician, a teacher, a
  nurse, a family member) → a [member account](/docs/sharing/members) with the
  right role.
- **Someone who should come to you** (you'd rather approve people than collect
  details and hand out links) → turn on
  [membership requests](/docs/sharing/members#membership-requests) and approve
  each one with the right role.
- **A screen that shows just your current glucose** (a bedside clock, a tablet on
  the counter) → a [clock](/docs/sharing/clock), opened by its own unguessable
  link.

<Callout type="tip" title="Share the least, for the shortest time">
  If two options would both work, pick the narrower one. A guest link that expires
  on its own is easier to live with than a public link you have to remember to
  switch off, and a Viewer role shows far less than an Administrator one.
</Callout>

## Turning access back off

Every option here is reversible, and all but the clock are reversed from
**Settings > Sharing & Privacy**:

- **Public share link** — switch public access off, or **Regenerate** it. Either
  one stops the old link working immediately.
- **Guest link** — revoke it, or simply let it expire. A used code cannot be used
  a second time.
- **Member** — change their role to a narrower one, or remove them entirely.
- **Membership requests** — switch the toggle off, and no one new can ask. It
  doesn't affect anyone you have already approved.
- **Clock** — turned off separately. Delete it in the **Clock** section and its
  link stops working right away.

When in doubt, share the least you can for the shortest time you can — you can
always grant more later.
